# UI-only rule (CommitTrack)

**All visual UI code lives under `src/ui/` only.**

When editing files outside `src/ui/`:

- Import UI from `src/ui` or `src/ui/index.js` — never recreate Card, Modal, buttons, chips, or layout styles locally.
- Do **not** add Tailwind color/spacing classes (`bg-*`, `text-gray-*`, `rounded-xl`, `border-indigo-*`, `dark:*`, etc.).
- Outside `src/ui/`, `className` may only use **`ct-*`** layout tokens (e.g. `ct-page`, `ct-stack`) defined in `src/ui/styles/`.
- Do **not** add duplicate re-export shims like `src/components/Card.jsx`.

Reference palette (match product mockup): backgrounds `#0B1020` / `#121A2F`, cards `#1B233D`, accent `#7C5CFF`, success `#22C55E`, warning `#F59E0B`, danger `#EF4444`, text `#F5F7FA` / `#A8B2C7` / `#6E7B91`.

Run `npm run audit` before finishing work (full report: UI, lint, dead code, env, tests, production build). Use `npm run audit -- --strict` to fail on warnings too.

See `src/ui/ARCHITECTURE.md`.
